  "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#semiotic_projection_1",
  "@type": "SemioticProjection",
  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the visual material of the man",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the visual material of the elderly Black man in the image. The meme's overall intent and textual content ('when the weed man throw in a little extra') create an implicit identification where the viewer is encouraged to imagine themselves as the 'weed man' or as someone who would react to the scenario described. This projection is not explicit with deictic pronouns like 'you' or 'me', but it is implied through the meme's structure: the viewer is positioned as the recipient of the 'extra' or as the person who is being stereotyped as dishonest or greedy in the context of drug dealing. The visual material (the man) is the focal point onto which the user's identity is projected as the subject of the stereotype.",
  "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface",
  "extractedFrom": "74368",
